.TH "rtl_tcp_soapy" 1 "1.0.0" "rtl-sdr-soapy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rtl_tcp_soapy \- an rtl_tcp compatible I/Q spectrum server backed by SoapySDR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provides the same TCP wire protocol as
.BR rtl_tcp (1)
but uses a SoapySDR supported SDR device instead of an RTL2832 based
DVB-T receiver.  This allows unmodified rtl_tcp clients (gr-osmosdr,
gqrx, SDR#, ...) to use USRP, LimeSDR, PlutoSDR and other devices that
SoapySDR can talk to.  The samples are converted to the unsigned 8 bit
I/Q format expected by rtl_tcp clients, with zero represented by 127 or
128.
.LP
The device configuration selected on the command line is re-applied for
every new client, so a client that does not set the sample rate (several
DAB clients rely on the rtl_tcp default of 2048000 Hz) always starts from
a known state instead of inheriting the settings of the previous client.
.LP
The gain table advertised to clients is derived from the device's actual
gain range at startup, so the highest gain index selects the highest gain
the device supports.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B  rtl_tcp_soapy [OPTIONS]
.SH DEVICE OPTIONS
.IP "--args <args>"
SoapySDR device arguments, for example "driver=uhd".  When omitted the
first device found is used.
.IP "-c, --channel <n>"
RX channel index (default: 0).
.IP "-f, --freq <Hz>"
Initial center frequency (default: 100000000).
.IP "-s, --samplerate <Hz>"
Initial sample rate (default: 2048000).
.IP "-b, --bandwidth <Hz>"
RF filter bandwidth (default: driver default).
.IP "-g, --gain <dB>"
Initial gain in dB and enables manual gain mode.  When omitted automatic
gain control is used.
.IP "-T, --bias-tee"
Enable the bias tee at startup, when the device supports it.
.SH SERVER OPTIONS
.IP "--listen <addr>"
Listen address as host:port, :port or host.
.IP "-a, --addr <addr>"
Listen address (default: 127.0.0.1).
.IP "-p, --port <port>"
Listen port (default: 1234).
.SH COMPATIBILITY OPTIONS
.IP "--tuner-type <n>"
Spoofed RTL-SDR tuner type reported in the handshake (default: 5, R820T).
.IP "-D, --direct-sampling"
Accepted for compatibility and ignored.
.IP "-h, --help"
Show a help message.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP "rtl_tcp_soapy --args \"driver=uhd\" --listen 127.0.0.1:1234"
Serve a USRP on the default rtl_tcp port.
.IP "rtl_tcp_soapy --args \"driver=lime\" --listen 0.0.0.0:1234 -f 100M -s 2.048M"
Serve a LimeSDR on all interfaces at 100 MHz and 2.048 MSps.
.LP
Use the device argument 'rtl_tcp=<host>:<port>' in the OsmoSDR
(gr-osmosdr) source to receive samples in GRC and control the frequency,
gain and sample rate remotely.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rtl_tcp (1),
.BR rtl_sdr (1),
.BR rtl_test (1),
.BR rtl_fm (1)
